 ],
 "text": "Blue babies lacked oxygen, Vivian Thomas helped fix it, then went uncredited. Too little of their blood reached the lungs. A shunt rerouted an artery to the lungs, so more blood picked up oxygen. Thomas perfected it on about 200 dogs, then coached the surgeon. On paper, he was a janitor. The 1945 report left out his name. Lesson, practice where mistakes are safe, then guide the real thing. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
